---
title: Youvetsi (Greek Lamb Stew with Orzo)
serves: 6
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
---

Season the @lamb neck fillet, shoulder, or leg{0.5%kg}(cut into 1” chunks) with @salt and @black pepper{}.

In a #large heavy pan with a lid{}, heat @olive oil{3%tbsp} over medium-high heat until shimmering but not smoking. Add the lamb and cook for 7 to ~{10%minutes}, tossing regularly, until browned. Transfer the lamb to a large plate.

In the same pan, add the @onions{2%large}(finely chopped) and @garlic{4%cloves}(minced). Season with @salt. Cook for 3 to ~{5%minutes}, stirring regularly, until softened.

Return the lamb to the pan. Add the @red wine{250%ml}, @oregano{1%tsp}, @paprika{1%tsp}, @cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, @nutmeg{0.5%tsp}, and @bay leaf{1}. Cook until the wine has reduced by at least half, then add @water{250%ml} and the @chopped tomatoes{2%tins}. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat to low. Cover and let simmer for 45 minutes to ~{1%hour}, or until the lamb is cooked through.

> Stop at this point if preparing the day before.

Stir in the @orzo pasta (or other small shapes){250%ml} and cover the pan. Let it cook for another ~{20%minutes} or until the orzo has cooked through and most of the moisture has been absorbed.

Garnish with @parsley{0.5%cup}(chopped) and crumbled @feta cheese{}.